# CWYD-18 — rate limits at the web server (DOM-27). Run against `docker compose up --build --wait`
# (VS Code / Cursor REST Client, or JetBrains HTTP Client). Limits are per client address and
# apply only through the web server (:8080); direct calls to the API (:8000) are not limited.
# Defaults: questions 10/min, burst 5, 2 at a time; uploads 6/min, burst 3 (RATE_LIMIT_* in .env).

# From inside the dev container the published ports live on the host daemon
# (docker-outside-of-docker): set @host = host.docker.internal there.
@host = localhost
@web = http://{{host}}:8080

### Question: send it 7 times within a few seconds. The first 6 (1 + burst 5) reach the API
# (200, or 409 no_ready_documents without Ready documents); the 7th answers
# 429 {"code":"rate_limited","detail":"Too many requests. Try again in a minute."}
# with Retry-After: 60, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy and X-Frame-Options.
POST {{web}}/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What is the coworking reimbursement limit?"}

### Upload: send it 5 times within a few seconds (the same file answers 200 after the first 202).
# The first 4 (1 + burst 3) reach the API; the 5th answers 429 rate_limited with Retry-After.
POST {{web}}/api/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="office-handbook.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ../../backend/tests/fixtures/documents/office-handbook.txt
--cwyd--

### Listing and status polling are never limited: 200 however often it is sent
GET {{web}}/api/documents

# Shell loops (not REST-client requests):
#   for i in $(seq 8); do curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} ' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#     -d '{"question":"What is the expense limit?"}' {{web}}/api/chat; done; echo
#   -> 409 409 409 409 409 409 429 429   (no Ready documents; 200 instead of 409 with one)
#   curl -s -D - -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"question":"q"}' {{web}}/api/chat
#   -> HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests ... Retry-After: 60 ... {"code":"rate_limited",...}
# Concurrent questions over RATE_LIMIT_CHAT_CONNECTIONS (2) also get 429 while the first ones run.
